---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Calculate Your Mortgage Payment in the USA | bestfinancecalculator.com"
  description="Learn exactly how monthly mortgage payments are calculated in the USA, including principal, interest, property tax, insurance and HOA fees with real examples."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <!-- Back to Blog Link -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-brand hover:text-brand-hover transition-colors">
        <svg class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18" />
        </svg>
        Back to Blog
      </a>
    </div>

    <!-- Article Header -->
    <header class="mb-12">
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-full bg-brand/10 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-brand ring-1 ring-inset ring-brand/20">
        Mortgage Guide
      </span>
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold font-display tracking-tight text-main-text leading-tight">
        How to Calculate Your Mortgage Payment in the USA
      </h1>
      <div class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted-text border-b border-border pb-8">
        <span>Published: June 10, 2026</span>
        <span class="h-1 w-1 rounded-full bg-border"></span>
        <span>5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Article Content -->
    <article class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-muted-text space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
      <p class="text-lg text-main-text/80">
        If you are buying a home in the United States, understanding how your monthly mortgage payment is calculated can save you thousands of dollars. Most buyers only look at the interest rate, but your actual monthly payment has four components — principal, interest, property tax, and home insurance — commonly called PITI.
      </p>

      <!-- Section: The Basic Formula -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          The Basic Formula
        </h2>
        <p>
          Your core mortgage payment (principal and interest) is calculated using this formula:
        </p>
        <div class="my-6 p-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface text-center font-mono text-main-text overflow-x-auto text-lg">
          M = P [ r(1 + r)^n ] / [ (1 + r)^n - 1 ]
        </div>
        <p>
          Where <strong>P</strong> is your loan amount, <strong>r</strong> is your monthly interest rate (annual rate divided by 12), and <strong>n</strong> is your total number of payments (loan term in years multiplied by 12).
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: Real Example -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Real Example
        </h2>
        <p>
          Let's put this into perspective with a real-world home purchase scenario:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Home price:</strong> $400,000</li>
          <li><strong>Down payment:</strong> 20% ($80,000)</li>
          <li><strong>Loan amount:</strong> $320,000</li>
          <li><strong>Interest rate:</strong> 6.5%</li>
          <li><strong>Loan term:</strong> 30 years</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Using the formula above, your monthly principal and interest payment is <strong>$2,022</strong>. To get the total monthly housing cost, you must add average property tax ($400/month), home insurance ($100/month), and HOA fees ($150/month). Your final total monthly payment becomes <strong>$2,672</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: Why the Down Payment Matters -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Why the Down Payment Matters
        </h2>
        <p>
          A 20% down payment eliminates Private Mortgage Insurance (PMI), which typically costs 0.5% to 1.5% of the loan amount annually. On a $320,000 loan, that is up to $400 per month in extra costs. Putting down less than 20% significantly increases your monthly payment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: Fixed vs Adjustable Rate -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Fixed vs Adjustable Rate
        </h2>
        <p>
          A fixed rate mortgage keeps your principal and interest payment the same for the entire loan term. An adjustable rate mortgage (ARM) starts lower but can increase after an initial fixed period, typically 5 or 7 years. For most buyers in 2026, a fixed rate provides more financial certainty.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: How Extra Payments Help -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          How Extra Payments Help
        </h2>
        <p>
          Paying an extra $200 per month on a $320,000 loan at 6.5% over 30 years saves over $60,000 in interest and cuts 4 years off your loan term. Use our free mortgage calculator to see exactly how much you can save with extra payments.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Section: Use Our Free Calculator -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
          Use Our Free Calculator
        </h2>
        <p>
          Our mortgage calculator handles all of this math instantly. Enter your home price, down payment, interest rate, and loan term and get your complete monthly payment breakdown including property tax, insurance, and HOA fees in real time. No signup required.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Call to Action Box -->
    <div class="mt-12 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface p-8 text-center space-y-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold font-display text-main-text">
        Ready to project your mortgage costs?
      </h3>
      <p class="text-muted-text max-w-lg mx-auto text-sm">
        Use our interactive tool to calculate interest charges, property taxes, insurance, and the power of making extra payments in real-time.
      </p>
      <div>
        <a 
          href="/mortgage-calculator" 
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-brand hover:bg-brand-hover px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition-colors duration-200"
        >
          Open Mortgage Calculator
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
